From 6c01613e628ae16b73b7628627b63a93d574f55e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 11:11:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add real-time Meta Pixel/CAPI events log to admin (replaces
 Meta Events Manager)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Remove hardcoded Meta Pixel ID + CAPI access token fallback from
  lib/metaCapi.js (was committed in plaintext, now env-var only). Rotate the
  leaked token in Meta Events Manager and set META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN /
  NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID in hosting env vars.
- Log every CAPI send attempt (success/fail, Meta response, match quality)
  to a new pixel_events Supabase table (scripts/supabase-pixel-events.sql).
- Add lib/trackEvent.js: shared client helper that fires the browser pixel
  and server CAPI together with a matching event_id for deduplication.
- Wire up ViewContent (product page), AddToCart (add to bag), and
  InitiateCheckout (checkout load) tracking — previously only PageView and
  Purchase were actually implemented despite the dashboard claiming all five
  were tracked.
- Add Admin > Events page (new sidebar item) showing a live, filterable log
  of every event with real delivery/match status.
- Replace the dashboard's fabricated funnel numbers (estimated from order
  count) and the external "View Live Events in Meta Events Manager" link
  with real counts from pixel_events and an internal "View Live Events in
  Admin" button.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012kxvbkNp2gRcjq3vbu29T4
